    "connector": "Every one of three real physical replacements enforces foreign_keys=1 and configured busy_timeout. Cancellation after expired native Open starts zero initialization SQL. Cancellation after the first successful initialization PRAGMA never lends a partially initialized connection. Default/no-deadline behavior and uncontended zero-wait initialization beyond 1ms succeed with the original fixed 1s work budget; zero-wait original-context clipping and immediate admission under quarantine are independently exercised.",
    "captured_outputs": "Actual late RETURNING rows separately exercise AckRelayDecision, DenyRelayTimeout and AckCursorDecision: bounded caller sees zero outputs/Busy, then finite release plus safe lease/durable full-request inspection proves no fabricated ack or late committed mutation.",
    "cli": "Existing real-child CLI outcome table remains unchanged: ordinary expired ErrStoreBusy produces exactly one durable ad.decide.called before normal process exit. New Linux child test fills a real FIFO, blocks real audit Write, requires 500ms teardown within the original CLI allowance, pending/context-expired stderr, unchanged structured Busy verdict and durable undecided request, and zero fabricated/duplicate durable events after child exit. Parent trail singleton never closed.",
    "setup_fixture": "Prepared the observed physical connection before starting the same original 100ms context; all canceled/deadline/ordinary-I/O classifications retain exact setup1/BEGIN0/COMMIT0, original 1.1s physical guard, discard/replacement and reuse checks. Previously omitted deadline leaf included in final broad targeted selectors.",
    "store_recovery": "Original held-call waits/physical/no-mutation/timeout checks retained for all 15 leaves. Fresh positive recovery explicitly uses dispatch-required 100ms, zero remains zero. Real COMMIT-start/success events classify confirmed success, Busy with zero COMMIT/no mutation, or explicit in-flight/unconfirmed COMMIT followed by safe-lease durable inspection. No replay. Separate nine fresh fixtures require unconditional success with DefaultLockWait and verify each relevant durable effect.",
    "api": "All original 23 parallel agent/busy/phase physical leaves retain 500ms/1.5s and real original SQL context. A successful actual Store verdict return is the confirmed-COMMIT event; only then is the external holder acquired, with explicit holder-ready event. Precommit exhaustion and unconfirmed COMMIT have distinct causal assertions and durable inspection; neither is called postcommit lock evidence. Exact FallenBack/no-attempt and postcommit allow/not_confirmed are four parallel controlled policy companions using established DecideWithinForTest. Original real physical callers do not use that seam.",
    "tmux": "Independent owned sentinel session established before persistence fault; kept alive through public Kill/FindMissing/Status and fresh recovery spawn/pause, asserted alive afterward. No retry of public Kill and no reinterpretation of unknown tmux replies.",
    "relay": "Raw holder setup uses busy_timeout=0 and finite context/event loop ending at the original persisted SettledAt minus existing 4s reserve. holderReady must precede that immutable instant; trigger dropped under held transaction. Original timer, no output bytes, no delivered_at, durable allow and unchanged settled_at assertions retained."
